+## Native files
+
+`adapter.py` implements the native `program(settings)` and
+`generate(seed, settings, demos, queries)` contract. It loads the retained
+`orientation.py` implementation by exact adjacent path, so another task's
+cached module cannot supply the rule. `promotion.json` declares four settings,
+the exact canonical default, 2–6 demonstrations, 1–4 queries, and three demos
+for native qualification. `audit.py` is a reusable protected-Racket
+learnability/export audit.
+
+The adapter accepts only exact integer seeds in `0..2**63-1`, 2–6
+demonstrations, and 1–4 queries. Settings must contain exactly one declared
+`orientation`. It returns `train`, `test`, and `program_solution`; the native
+qualification worker independently executes every label through protected
+Racket.
+
+## Episode construction
+
+Inputs are matched across settings. Demonstrations are selected constructively
+from lawful production-generator scenes: the minimum two-demo teaching set must
+refute every declared canonical shortcut under every orientation. All retained
+inputs also produce four distinct orientation outputs. Extra demonstrations are
+lawful distinct fillers from the same pool.
+
+Queries use a stable prefix. Query 1 is an ordinary production-generator scene,
