 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## 2026-10-24 bounded learnability finding
+
+A produced-domain three-demo lesson is ambiguous against the executable rival
+`skip_when_disconnected_pockets_exist`: apply the intended unavoidable-shortest-
+path rule only when every open cell is reachable from the start; otherwise
+return the input unchanged. For seed 0/default difficulty, demos at indices
+5, 6, 7 are `dead_end_contrast`, `public_3`, and `many_paths_few_gates`, all
+with zero unreachable open cells, so the rival matches every protected-Racket
+label. The next generated query at index 8 is `disconnected_pockets`; canonical
+Racket still marks four unavoidable shortest-path blanks while the rival leaves
+the grid unchanged.
+
+Reusable reproducer: `workspace/learnability_probe.py`; source-bound evidence:
+`checks/d4f2f542248a/learnability.json`. A focused regression fixes the exact
+window in `tests/test_learnability_probe.py`. Suggested repair is to ensure a
+disconnected-pocket demonstration is visible before such a query without
+increasing the demo count. No generator source change was applied in this
+optional review; the owner should choose and verify any integration.
+
+## 2026-10-24 portable test repair
+
+The optional review also repaired the retained test's fixed `__file__/parents`
+lookup. Canonical and base-authority data now resolve from
+`reviewer_support.find_root()` / `canonical_path()`, so the same test works in
+the repository and staged runtime layouts. The staged runner passed its
+portability preflight and the first 55 tests; 81/82 tests pass in a targeted
+run. The sole remaining census performs 1,760 expensive generations and did not
+finish within a separate 20-minute bound; it produced no assertion failure and
+was not changed. This performance limit is separate from the learnability
+finding and from generator correctness.
